From 0195cc0701a0bfe3a0cf1999b995e4a8d8ad4c99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:35:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/33] drm/gma500: build sgxfive transfer commands from the
 UAPI block

Turn a job's UAPI register block into the firmware's SGXMKIF_TRANSFERCMD:
the 41 register words around the UAPI's load_flags, the coefficient-load
booleans, the pixel partitions, and the kernel-owned size, flags, fence
status and fence id; a dummy job carries only the latter. Check the block:
the addresses the pixel pipe fetches from or runs code at must be in a user
heap, the 3D request base must be 1 MiB aligned, and unsupported fields must
be clear. KUnit pins the layout and the checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/Makefile               |   5 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_cmd.c  |  90 ++++++++++++
 .../gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_job_test.c | 130 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_priv.h |   4 +
 4 files changed, 227 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_cmd.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/sgxfive_job_test.c

